1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:01,250
Here's a tricky one.

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:05,060
The letters OO make two different sounds.

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:09,770
Most of the time, OO makes a long sound.

4
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:15,740
OO, like in moon, zoo and food.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,400
But some words use a short OO sound.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,520
OO, like in book, good and foot.

7
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,080
Here's the tricky part.

8
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:31,580
OO doesn't always sound the same.

9
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,520
So when you're reading, try the long sound first.

10
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:39,480
If it doesn't sound right, try the short sound.

11
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:41,940
Here's a helpful hint.

12
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:45,500
OO before K is often short.

13
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,720
Book, look, cook.

14
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:52,820
But that's not always true.

15
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:55,840
Good and foot are short too.

16
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,560
So keep practising and trust your ears.

17
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:02,000
Here are some examples.

18
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:10,760
Long OO, moon, food, zoo, spoon.

19
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:19,340
Short OO, book, good, foot, wood.

20
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:22,060
Now it's your turn.

21
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:25,720
Good, long or short?

22
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:29,220
It's short, good.

23
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,560
No K but it's still short.

24
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:37,920
Remember, OO is long most of the time, like moon.

25
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:41,680
But some words are short, like book.

26
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,860
The more you read, the easier it gets.

27
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:50,140
Read more tricky words in the English learning app.

28
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,360
Listen, try.
